# RTL and Farsi

The project is **Persian (Farsi)**. Use RTL layout and RTL-aware styling everywhere.

## Root Layout

In `app/layout.tsx` (or the root layout):

```tsx
<html lang="fa" dir="rtl">
```

Load a Farsi-friendly font if needed (e.g. Vazirmatn via next/font or a similar approach).

## Tailwind: Prefer RTL-Aware Utilities

Use logical / direction-agnostic utilities so styles work in RTL:

| Avoid (directional) | Prefer (logical) |
|---------------------|------------------|
| `ml-*`, `mr-*`      | `ms-*`, `me-*`   |
| `pl-*`, `pr-*`      | `ps-*`, `pe-*`   |
| `left-*`, `right-*` | `start-*`, `end-*` |
| `text-left`         | `text-start`     |
| `border-l`, `border-r` | `border-s`, `border-e` |

## Examples

```tsx
// Good: logical margins in RTL
<div className="ms-4 me-2 ps-3 pe-4">

// Bad: fixed left/right (wrong side in RTL)
<div className="ml-4 mr-2 pl-3 pr-4">
```

```tsx
// Good: alignment
<p className="text-start">...</p>

// Bad
<p className="text-left">...</p>
```

When converting from LTR samples, replace `left`/`right` and `ml`/`mr`/`pl`/`pr` with the logical equivalents so the UI flips correctly for Farsi.
